  "reasoning": "The patient presents with itchy red spots all over the body, accompanied by fever, headache, and exhaustion. These symptoms strongly align with chicken pox, which classically begins with systemic symptoms like fever, headache, and fatigue, followed by an itchy rash. While dengue also features fever, headache, and a rash, reference cases consistently link it to severe body pain and vomiting, which are absent here. Allergy typically presents with prominent respiratory symptoms such as sneezing and a runny nose, which are not reported. Fungal infection usually involves discolored patches or distinct ball-like pimples, unlike the uniform red spots described. Therefore, chicken pox is the most accurate diagnosis based on the symptom profile and matching reference cases.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]chicken pox[/DIAGNOSIS]"
